# Per-repo release values, sourced by scripts/release/_lib.sh. preflight,
# postflight and sync-dev are separate entry points, so a value declared in one
# script is missing from the other two; this file is the one place all three
# read.
#
# This bundle has no Cargo.toml: its version lives in VERSION and its release
# notes in the root CHANGELOG.md, which are what the scripts read when nothing
# here names a manifest or a changelog. So it sets neither RELEASE_MANIFEST nor
# RELEASE_CHANGELOG. It has no deployed surface, so STAGING_URL_DEFAULT and
# PROD_URL_DEFAULT stay unset too.

# How drift.sh gate 0 compares a manifest carrier (Cargo.toml, package.json,
# pyproject.toml) the last release changed. "lines", the default, holds base to
# the release's whole change to the manifest. "version" checks only that base
# declares the release's version or a newer one: set it when every release ships
# less than dev, such as a release branch that strips a feature dev keeps.
# Changelogs stay on the line check either way.
# DRIFT_MANIFEST_COMPARE="version"
